Why Parallelize Parsing? 

Assume: 

CSV File = 5 seconds  Excel File = 5 seconds  JSON File = 5 seconds API Data = 5 seconds 

Sequential Processing: 

CSV -> 5 sec  Excel -> 5 sec  JSON -> 5 sec API -> 5 sec 

Total = 20 sec 

Parallel Processing: 

CSV \ 

Excel \ 

JSON ---> Run Together 

API / 

  

Total ≈ 5 sec 

Parallel Parsing Using ThreadPoolExecutor 

import pandas as pd 

from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor  

def read_csv_file(): 

return pd.read_csv("employees.csv") 

def read_excel_file(): 

return pd.read_excel("employees.xlsx") 

def read_json_file(): 

return pd.read_json("employees.json") 

with ThreadPoolExecutor() as executor: 

csv_future = executor.submit(read_csv_file) 

excel_future = executor.submit(read_excel_file) 

json_future = executor.submit(read_json_file) 

csv_df = csv_future.result() 

excel_df = excel_future.result() 

json_df = json_future.result() 

final_df = pd.concat( 

[csv_df, excel_df, json_df], 

ignore_index=True 

) 

print(final_df.head()) 

Multiple files are parsed simultaneously. 

No need to wait for one file to finish before starting another. 

Reduces overall execution time. 

 

Parallel API Parsing Using Asyncio 

import asyncio 

import aiohttp 

async def fetch(session, url): 

async with session.get(url) as response: 

return await response.json() 

async def main(): 

urls = [ 

"https://api1.com", 

"https://api2.com", 

"https://api3.com" 

] 

async with aiohttp.ClientSession() as session: 

tasks = [ 

fetch(session, url) 

for url in urls 

]  

results = await asyncio.gather(*tasks) 

 return results 

results = asyncio.run(main()) 

 print(results) 

Sends multiple API requests simultaneously. 

Does not wait for one API response before calling the next. 

Best for I/O-bound tasks such as APIs. 

 

Why We Parallelize Parsing? 

Faster Execution    Multiple files or APIs are processed simultaneously. 

Better Resource Utilization      CPU and I/O resources are used efficiently. 

Reduced Waiting Time    One slow source does not block others. 

Faster ETL Pipelines    Extract phase becomes faster. 

Improved Scalability     Can process many files and APIs together. 

 

