How can we reduce token cost in LLM applications? 

Key techniques include: 

Writing short and specific prompts 

Limiting response length 

Using RAG instead of sending full documents 

Re-ranking retrieved chunks 

Redis caching for responses and embeddings 

Conversation summarization 

Deterministic routing before LLM calls 

Context compression 

Semantic caching 

Using smaller models for simple tasks 

One-Line Answer 

The best way to reduce token cost is to send only the most relevant context using RAG and re-ranking, avoid repeated LLM calls through Redis caching, summarize conversation history, and use concise prompts with controlled output length. 

 
